# No flash write while the USB audio is recorded and the music sounds (2026-11-09). A write turns the interrupts off a millisecond or more at a time, the
# USB audio's 1 ms packets go missing and the recording crackles and stutters; it was heard in a recording's first seconds with the auto-DJ, whose settings
# are written a moment after it starts. A setting changed while recording waits; it is written when the recording stops, or when the music has stopped
# and fallen silent.
seed 0
wait 3000
expect playing 1
expect store_writes 0
# recording: a DJ setting changed (DJ MOVES' Mood), left alone far past the usual moment: nothing written
usbrec 1
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 3
wait 100
expect fxpage 35
spin K1 1
wait 50
expect fxs96 1
tap FX
wait 20000
expect store_writes 0
# the recording stops: written
usbrec 0
waitfor store_writes 1 15000
# recording again, a setting changed: waits; the music stopped: not while its tails ring on in the recording (they did, at the stop), but once the output
# has been silent a moment (a missing packet's stand-in is silence too)
usbrec 1
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 3
wait 100
expect fxpage 35
spin K1 1
wait 50
expect fxs96 2
tap FX
wait 15000
expect store_writes 1
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 0
expect store_writes 1
waitfor store_writes 2 30000
